// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`infra CLI shows root help with registered top-level commands 1`] = `
"infra/x.x.x

Usage:
  $ infra <command> [options]

Commands:
  keeweb status                                  Show operational health of the KeeWeb deployment
    --verbose                                    Enable verbose output for all commands

  keeweb deploy                                  Trigger KeeWeb deployment. Default mode dispatches the GitHub Deploy KeeWeb workflow. Use --local to run apps/keeweb/deploy.sh directly from this repo.
    --local                                      Run local deployment using apps/keeweb/deploy.sh instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --nginx                                      Include nginx config deployment. Valid only with --local and passed through to deploy.sh as --nginx. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Print planned actions without validating preconditions, executing deploy.sh, or triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)

  keeweb open                                    Open KeeWeb in the default browser
  agent setup                                    Configure generalized Fro Bot agent model-credential setup and GitHub secrets and variables.
    --key [key]                                  Existing CLIProxyAPI API key value. When provided, setup skips key creation and reuses this key for GitHub secrets.
    --repo [repo]                                Target GitHub repository in owner/repo format. Skips the repository prompt when provided.
    --harness [harness]                          Harness template to configure. Choose opencode, claude-code, or generic. Generic remains interactive-only.
    --providers [providers]                      Comma-separated list of providers to enable. Default: anthropic. Supported values: anthropic, openai, opencode-go. Example: --providers anthropic,openai
    --model [model]                              Override the default model. Must be provider-prefixed and lowercase. Required when multiple providers selected. Examples: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6, openai/gpt-4o, opencode-go/glm-5.3
    --force                                      Overwrite existing GitHub secrets and variables without prompting.
    --dry-run                                    Print the plan without applying any changes.
    --verify-smoke                               Run a smoke test against the proxy after setup completes.
    --ack-key-reuse                              Acknowledge that --key matches the bearer token inside the existing OPENCODE_AUTH_JSON. Required in non-interactive mode when --key is supplied for a repo with existing OPENCODE_AUTH_JSON. (default: false)

  agent storage                                  Verify the provisioned S3 handoff and wire non-secret GitHub storage variables. AWS readback requires AGENT_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and AGENT_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY and ignores ambient AWS_* values.
    --repo [repo]                                Target GitHub repository in owner/repo format.
    --manifest [manifest]                        Handoff manifest path, or - to read JSON from stdin. (default: -)
    --plan                                       Verify and report storage writes without mutating GitHub.
    --dry-run                                    Alias for --plan.

  agent storage teardown                         Unwire S3 variables and remove the repo-scoped storage resources.
    --repo [repo]                                Target GitHub repository in owner/repo format.
    --manifest [manifest]                        Handoff manifest path, or - to read JSON from stdin. (default: -)
    --purge-state                                Delete versioned session-prefix objects instead of retaining them.
    --plan                                       Read back and report teardown actions without mutating.

  cliproxy status                                Show operational health of CLIProxyAPI and its management endpoints.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI health checks. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Management API key. Falls back to CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY when omitted.
    --api-key [key]                              Downstream API key (bearer) for the upstream provider-auth probe. Falls back to CLIPROXY_API_KEY. Skipped when absent.
    --verbose                                    Enable verbose output for all commands

  cliproxy deploy                                Deploy CLIProxyAPI. Default mode triggers the GitHub Deploy CLIProxy workflow, while --local runs apps/cliproxy/src/deploy.ts directly with Bun.
    --local                                      Run local deployment with Bun using apps/cliproxy/src/deploy.ts instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --force-config                               Force upload config.yaml even if it exists on the server. WARNING: overwrites runtime API keys and settings. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Validate deploy prerequisites and print planned actions without executing local deploy or dispatching workflow. (default: false)

  cliproxy config get                            Fetch current CLIProxyAPI config as JSON.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI management requests. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Management API key. Falls back to CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY when omitted.
    --output [file]                              Write config JSON to a file instead of stdout. File permissions set to 0600 (owner-read-only).
    --json                                       Output raw JSON instead of aligned key: value columns.

  cliproxy config set <field> <value>            Update a mutable CLIProxyAPI config field via its dedicated management endpoint.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI management requests. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Management API key. Falls back to CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY when omitted.

  cliproxy keys list                             List CLIProxyAPI API keys from the management API.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI management requests. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Management API key. Falls back to CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY when omitted.
    --json                                       Output raw JSON array instead of a numbered list.

  cliproxy keys add <key>                        Add an API key by fetching current keys, appending the value, and replacing full key set.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI management requests. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Management API key. Falls back to CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY when omitted.

  cliproxy keys remove <key>                     Remove an API key via management API endpoint query parameter.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI management requests. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Management API key. Falls back to CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY when omitted.

  cliproxy login <provider>                      Run provider login on the remote CLIProxyAPI host. Supported providers: claude, codex.
    --host [host]                                CLIProxyAPI droplet host for SSH execution. Falls back to CLIPROXY_DOMAIN or cliproxy.fro.bot.

  cliproxy models [provider]                     List the models CLIProxyAPI serves.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  API key (bearer). Falls back to CLIPROXY_API_KEY when omitted.
    --verbose                                    Show owned_by and created date for each model.

  cliproxy monitor                               Reconcile Anthropic and OpenCode Go provider routes, each with its own canonical GitHub issue and transition-only Discord alerts. Requires CLIPROXY_API_KEY, CLIPROXY_AUTH_MONITOR_DISCORD_WEBHOOK, GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_REPOSITORY, GITHUB_ACTOR, and GITHUB_REPOSITORY_OWNER environment variables; prefer the cliproxy-auth-monitor.yaml GitHub Actions entrypoint for scheduled or synthetic validation.
    --validation [mode]                          Validation mode (live, synthetic-dead, or synthetic-healthy): live probes Anthropic and OpenCode Go; synthetic modes are owner-only isolated Anthropic test transitions. (default: live)

  cliproxy open                                  Launch CLIProxyAPI TUI dashboard via SSH.
    --host [host]                                SSH host for CLIProxyAPI server. Falls back to CLIPROXY_DOMAIN or cliproxy.fro.bot.

  cliproxy reset-quota [auth-index]              Reset the quota for one CLIProxyAPI auth record, or list valid auth indexes.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for CLIProxyAPI management requests. Falls back to CLIPROXY_URL or https://cliproxy.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Management API key. Falls back to CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY when omitted.
    --list                                       List auth records and their auth indexes without resetting quota.
    --json                                       Output auth records as JSON when used with --list.

  cliproxy setup                                 Interactively onboard a GitHub repository to CLIProxyAPI by creating or reusing a key and wiring the required GitHub secrets and variables.
    --key [key]                                  Existing CLIProxyAPI API key value. When provided, setup skips key creation and reuses this key for GitHub secrets.
    --repo [repo]                                Target GitHub repository in owner/repo format. Skips the repository prompt when provided.
    --harness [harness]                          Harness template to configure. Choose opencode, claude-code, or generic. Generic remains interactive-only.
    --providers [providers]                      Comma-separated list of providers to enable. Default: anthropic. Supported values: anthropic, openai, opencode-go. Example: --providers anthropic,openai
    --model [model]                              Override the default model. Must be provider-prefixed and lowercase. Required when multiple providers selected. Examples: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6, openai/gpt-4o, opencode-go/glm-5.3
    --force                                      Overwrite existing GitHub secrets and variables without prompting.
    --dry-run                                    Print the plan without applying any changes.
    --verify-smoke                               Run a smoke test against the proxy after setup completes.
    --ack-key-reuse                              Acknowledge that --key matches the bearer token inside the existing OPENCODE_AUTH_JSON. Required in non-interactive mode when --key is supplied for a repo with existing OPENCODE_AUTH_JSON. (default: false)

  broker status                                  Show operational health of the credential broker.
    --url [url]                                  Base URL for broker health checks. Falls back to BROKER_DOMAIN, BROKER_HOST, or https://broker.fro.bot.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the broker host. Falls back to BROKER_DOMAIN when omitted.
    --verbose                                    Enable verbose output for all commands

  broker deploy                                  Deploy the credential broker. Default mode triggers the GitHub Deploy Broker workflow, while --local runs apps/broker/src/deploy.ts directly with Bun.
    --local                                      Run local deployment with Bun using apps/broker/src/deploy.ts instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Validate deploy prerequisites and print planned actions without executing local deploy or dispatching workflow. (default: false)

  broker logs                                    Stream credential broker service logs via SSH.
    --tail [n]                                   Number of log lines to tail. (default: 100)
    --service [service]                          Docker Compose service name to stream logs from. (default: broker)
    --allow-ci                                   Allow log streaming in CI environments. Logs may contain sensitive broker data. (default: false)
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to BROKER_HOST when omitted.

  gateway status                                 Show operational health of the gateway deployment via docker compose ps.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to GATEWAY_HOST when omitted.
    --json                                       Output a single JSON object with ok, services and the structured workspace memory status.

  gateway deploy                                 Deploy the gateway. Default mode triggers the GitHub Deploy Gateway workflow, while --local runs apps/gateway deploy directly with Bun.
    --local                                      Run local deployment with Bun using apps/gateway instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Validate deploy prerequisites and print planned actions without executing local deploy or dispatching workflow. (default: false)
    --force-recreate                             Force recreate containers. Forwarded only in local mode. (default: false)

  gateway logs [service]                         Stream logs from a gateway service via SSH and docker compose.
    --tail [n]                                   Number of log lines to tail from each service. (default: 100)
    --allow-ci                                   Allow log streaming in CI environments. Logs may contain sensitive credentials. (default: false)
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to GATEWAY_HOST when omitted.

  gateway backup                                 Back up the mitmproxy CA certificate and private key from the gateway Docker volume to a local tarball. The output contains the CA private trust anchor — treat it as sensitive material.
    --output [file]                              Local path to write the CA tarball. File permissions are set to 0600 after writing. (default: apps/gateway/.local/mitmproxy-ca.tar)
    --include-ca                                 Include the mitmproxy CA certificate and private key in the backup. Currently the only supported backup target. (default: true)

  gateway restore                                Restore the mitmproxy CA certificate and private key from a local tarball into the gateway Docker volume. Restarts mitmproxy and gateway services after restore and confirms byte-equal content before reporting success.
    --input <file>                               Path to the tarball produced by \`gateway backup --include-ca\`. (required)
    --include-ca                                 Restore the mitmproxy CA certificate and private key. Currently the only supported restore target. (default: true)

  umami status                                   Show operational health of the Umami analytics deployment via docker compose ps.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to UMAMI_DOMAIN when omitted.

  umami deploy                                   Deploy Umami analytics. Default mode triggers the GitHub Deploy Umami workflow, while --local runs apps/umami deploy directly with Bun.
    --local                                      Run local deployment with Bun using apps/umami instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Validate deploy prerequisites and print planned actions without executing local deploy or dispatching workflow. (default: false)

  umami logs [service]                           Stream logs from an Umami service via SSH and docker compose.
    --tail [n]                                   Number of log lines to tail from each service. (default: 100)
    --allow-ci                                   Allow log streaming in CI environments. Logs may contain sensitive credentials. (default: false)
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to UMAMI_DOMAIN when omitted.

  dashboard status                               Show operational health of the dashboard deployment via docker compose ps.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to DASHBOARD_DOMAIN when omitted.

  dashboard deploy                               Deploy the dashboard. Default mode triggers the GitHub Deploy Dashboard workflow, while --local runs apps/dashboard deploy directly with Bun.
    --local                                      Run local deployment with Bun using apps/dashboard instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Validate deploy prerequisites and print planned actions without executing local deploy or dispatching workflow. (default: false)
    --image-version <version>                    CalVer version to deploy (e.g. 2026.06.47). Remote-only. Triggers the versioned release path and requires dashboard environment approval. Must match YYYY.MM.N. Forwarded as -f version=<value> to gh workflow run.
    --digest <digest>                            Expected sha256 digest (e.g. sha256:abc...def). Remote-only. Requires --image-version. When set, the workflow fails if GHCR resolves the tag to a different digest. Must match sha256:<64 hex chars>.

  dashboard logs [service]                       Stream logs from a dashboard service via SSH and docker compose.
    --tail [n]                                   Number of log lines to tail from each service. (default: 100)
    --allow-ci                                   Allow log streaming in CI environments. Logs may contain sensitive credentials. (default: false)
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to DASHBOARD_DOMAIN when omitted.

  vpn status                                     Show operational health of the VPN box via SSH and wg show.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to VPN_HOST when omitted.

  vpn deploy                                     Deploy the VPN. Default mode triggers the GitHub Deploy VPN workflow, while --local runs apps/vpn deploy directly with Bun.
    --local                                      Run local deployment with Bun using apps/vpn instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Validate deploy prerequisites and print planned actions without executing local deploy or dispatching workflow. (default: false)
    --force-server-key                           Force regeneration of the server WireGuard keypair. WARNING: invalidates all existing client configs. (default: false)

  vpn logs                                       Stream WireGuard VPN logs via SSH and journalctl.
    --tail [n]                                   Number of log lines to tail. (default: 100)
    --allow-ci                                   Allow log streaming in CI environments. Logs may contain sensitive VPN data. (default: false)
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to VPN_HOST when omitted.

  vpn client add <name>                          Add a new VPN client peer. Generates a keypair, assigns a tunnel IP, writes the client .conf to apps/vpn/clients/, and syncs the roster to the VPN_PEERS GitHub secret (best-effort).
    --split-tunnel [cidrs]                       Comma-separated CIDRs for split-tunnel routing. Defaults to 0.0.0.0/0 (full tunnel).
    --dns [dns]                                  DNS server for the client config.
    --server-pubkey [key]                        Server public key. Falls back to VPN_SERVER_PUBKEY env var.
    --endpoint [host]                            VPN server endpoint (IP or hostname). Falls back to VPN_HOST env var.

  vpn client list                                List all VPN client peers from peers.json.
  vpn client remove <name>                       Remove a VPN client peer from peers.json and sync the roster to the VPN_PEERS GitHub secret (best-effort). Run \`infra vpn deploy\` to revoke access.
  traces status                                  Show operational health of the trace stack: compose service states and the health reporter verdict, read over SSH.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.
    --json                                       Output one JSON object with ok, services and the reporter detail.

  traces deploy                                  Deploy the trace collection stack. Default mode triggers the GitHub Deploy Traces workflow, while --local runs apps/traces/src/deploy.ts directly with Bun.
    --local                                      Run local deployment with Bun using apps/traces/src/deploy.ts instead of triggering GitHub Actions. (default: false)
    --dry-run                                    Validate deploy prerequisites and print planned actions without executing local deploy or dispatching workflow. (default: false)

  traces logs [service]                          Stream logs from a trace-stack service via SSH and docker compose.
    --tail [n]                                   Number of log lines to tail from the service. (default: 100)
    --allow-ci                                   Allow log streaming in CI environments. Logs can contain trace content. (default: false)
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces open                                    Open an SSH tunnel to Langfuse (localhost:3000) and Grafana (localhost:3001). Neither has a public hostname.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces ingest hold                             Emergency close: hold the ingest route (every ingest path answers 503) and prove it from outside the host.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces ingest open                             Open the ingest route. Refuses unless the health reporter verdict is passing and no deploy is running or unfinished; proves the route is live from outside.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces ingest status                           Show the configured ingest state, the state seen from outside the host, and the health verdict.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces sender add <group>                      Issue a sender token for marcusrbrown, fro-bot or workstation. Writes it to the host, proves it is accepted, then delivers it once: to a GitHub Actions secret (TRACES_INGEST_TOKEN by default) or, for workstation, to this terminal.
    --repo [repo]                                OWNER/REPO to set the Actions secret on (repeatable).
    --org [org]                                  Organisation to set the Actions secret on, visible to the --org-repo repositories only.
    --org-repo [repo]                            Repository name (no owner) that may read the organisation secret (repeatable).
    --secret-name [name]                         Secret name. Default TRACES_INGEST_TOKEN.
    --print                                      Print a workstation token even when standard output is not a terminal.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces sender list                             List sender tokens per group: fingerprint and creation date. Never token text.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces sender revoke [group] [fingerprint]     Remove one sender token and prove it is now refused. With --all (no group, no fingerprint): make every group file deny-all (one void line, no real token) and prove every old token is refused on its private receiver.
    --all                                        Make every group token file deny-all. Proves over ssh only, never through the public hostname.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces reader add <consumer>                   Issue a reader token for a consumer (lower-case name). Writes it to the host, proves both agent routes accept it, then delivers it once: to a GitHub Actions secret (TRACES_READER_TOKEN by default) with --repo, otherwise to a 0600 file on this machine.
    --repo [repo]                                OWNER/REPO to set the Actions secret on (repeatable).
    --secret-name [name]                         Secret name. Default TRACES_READER_TOKEN.
    --file [path]                                Workstation token file. Default ~/.config/infra/traces-reader-<consumer>.token.
    --print                                      Show the token on this terminal instead of writing a file. Refused when not a terminal.
    --replace                                    Replace the consumer's existing token: install the new one, deliver it, then remove the old.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces reader list                             List reader tokens per consumer: fingerprint and date. Never token text.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces reader revoke [consumer] [fingerprint]  Remove every reader token of a consumer, or one by fingerprint, and prove both routes now answer 401. With --all (no consumer, no fingerprint): make the file deny-all, the reader kill switch.
    --all                                        Make the reader token file deny-all and prove every old token is refused.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces reader backend langfuse                 Install or rotate the Langfuse Viewer key the reader gate reads with. Prompts for the pair without echo, proves it on the host (reads; REST and MCP writes refused by role), then switches it in and keeps the old pair until --confirm-old-revoked.
    --confirm-old-revoked                        Prove Langfuse refuses the previous pair (delete it in the UI first), then delete it from the host.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces reader backend grafana                  Create or rotate the Grafana service-account token (agent-reader, Viewer) on the host. The key never leaves the host: only ids are printed. Proves a Grafana MCP read through the gate, then deletes every other token.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  traces reader backend status                   Report each reader backend credential as placeholder, installed or pending old-key revocation. Never prints a value.
    --key [key]                                  Environment variable name holding the SSH host. Falls back to TRACES_HOST, then traces.fro.bot.

  status                                         Show status of all deployments
    --json                                       Output a schema-versioned JSON envelope: schemaVersion, generatedAt, and one entry per app with typed observations (id, kind, result, observedAt, source) and facts. The gateway workspace memory status is in facts.workspace.

  status snapshot                                Take one public-safe status sample and merge it into the 90-day history directory. Runs only the public HTTPS probes, the TCP connect to the VPN box on port 22 (address from VPN_PROBE_HOST, never printed or recorded), the GitHub Deployments reader and the auth monitor reader (GITHUB_TOKEN or GH_TOKEN, read-only); it uses no SSH session and no deploy secrets. Stages every file as a temp file before renaming any into place; any invariant violation exits non-zero and writes nothing. Prints counts only. Exits 0 once the snapshot is written, even when observations are fail or unknown, because those are data. CLI-only: not exposed over MCP.
    --history <dir>                              History directory holding meta.json and apps/<app>.json. It must already contain a valid history unless --bootstrap is given. (required)
    --bootstrap                                  Create the history and its first sample. Fails if meta.json or any app file already exists; without this flag a missing history fails.
    --now [iso]                                  UTC ISO timestamp (for example 2026-11-01T12:00:00Z) to use as the sample time and the 90-day trim reference instead of the clock. Intended for tests and replays.

  status history-locate                          Find the newest usable status-history artifact for the snapshot workflow. Needs GITHUB_TOKEN or GH_TOKEN (read-only, actions: read) and reads GITHUB_REPOSITORY. Prints exactly "found run-id=<id>" or "empty" and exits 0; any API error, truncated listing or exhausted call budget exits non-zero, so an outage is never mistaken for an empty history. When GITHUB_OUTPUT is set it also appends state= and run-id= lines. CLI-only: not exposed over MCP.
  mcp                                            Start a stdio MCP server exposing all CLI commands as tools for coding agents

Options:
  --verbose      Enable verbose output for all commands
  -h, --help     Display this message
  -v, --version  Display version number
"
`;
